A||||11||gomobile||Removing DEW Stripts||||1||
Z||000000||gomobile||08-24-2001||09:59 AM||||I am in the process of removing all the DEW stripts but I have been made aware that it will be almost impossible to remove the outer dew due to closeness of the window let alone the small screw that holds them (ie; no room to manever inside). Any ideas anyone? Has anyone remove them due and if so what did it take without having to remove the WINDOW!||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||08-24-2001||10:10 AM||||It's a popular problem. <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>Rodney Dickman</A> makes a tool to remove those screws.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||08-24-2001||11:12 AM||||Others have had good success with cutting off or filing down a phillips bit to make it very short and then JB Welding it into the jaws of a cheapo open end wrench.  Look at Rodney's tool and you will get an idea of what you need.  I had a friend weld a shortened bit to a flat steel bar that I then wrapped in tape to keep it from scratching the windows.<p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 08-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mickey_Moose||08-24-2001||11:16 AM||||...or you could just buy an offset driver from most tool stores.<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000004||starfighter007@msn.com||08-24-2001||01:26 PM||||you know I was waiting for the tool that was getting passed around.But the more that I think about it I will probobly just take the glass out and install the strips. I feel that it will be less problematic this way||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaveL||08-24-2001||03:17 PM||||OK, here goes...you can get the old ones out including the two that are blocked by the window.  The trick is getting the new ones started and in. When I replacxed my dew wipes I didn't bother to replace the two middle screws that are blocked by the window, and haven't had any trouble with it since. The replacement dew strip from GM has metal embedded in it and is very stiff, stiff enough to function without the screws as long as the rest of them are in and tight. When I got down to removing the last 2 screws, I wedged a screwdriver behind the old strip and pried until it ripped out the holes around those screws and came loose. Got the middle screws out with a pair of needle nose pliars.<P>Good luck. Whatever you do, a certain amount of water will get inside the door, but there are drain holes for that already.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Galen||08-24-2001||04:20 PM||||I'll be the first to say it, do a search on it, theres some guy(with alot of anarchy following his post) that posted a way to get at it with no special tools. I have yet to try this cuz I can't afford a new a 25cent pack of gum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> but anyway hehe||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||08-25-2001||07:55 PM||||No Galen, you can't fix a cracked block with that stuff! :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>I'll be the first to say it, do a search on it, theres some guy(with alot of anarchy following his post) that posted a way to get at it with no special tools. I have yet to try this cuz I can't afford a new a 25cent pack of gum  :) but anyway hehe</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000008||jelly2m8||08-25-2001||09:29 PM||||Ya there is no need to buy any special tools to remove and replace the dew strips. Using a hacked up tool is a waste of time. I think the tread that was referred to is by DEVOTSHKA, do a search on it. <P> Basically all you need to do is remove both up-stops from the door, and loosen the fore-aft adjuster. Then you can roll the window waaay up and slide it back an inch or so. This lets you get at all 5  screws with a regular screw driver, from underneath the glass. Ever notice that the glass curved on the bottom?.............. Now you can find out why.<P> I did a write up on it, if I can find it, I'll post it. Its way quicker than the hacked tool method, and alot easier on that one last nerve............<BR>||||reg||1
